{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 640,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suppose you have a ball covered entirely with\nhair and you're trying to comb the hair so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4090,
    "dDurationMs": 2439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it lies flat everywhere along the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6529,
    "dDurationMs": 3821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the ball were a donut, or it existed in\ntwo dimensions, this would be easy!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10350,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in three dimensions?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11600,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, you're going to run into trouble."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13300,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of trouble."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14740,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A big hairy ball of trouble."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16820,
    "dDurationMs": 4369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because of a theorem in algebraic topology\ncalled the \"Hairy Ball Theorem\" (and yes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21189,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's it's real name) which unequivocally\nproves that at some point, the hair must stick"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25199,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26199,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now don't go wasting your time playing around\nwith a hairy ball trying to prove the theorem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29019,
    "dDurationMs": 2131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wrong - this is math we're talking about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31150,
    "dDurationMs": 2409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's proven - done - QED!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33559,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Technically speaking, what the Hairy Ball\ntheorem says is that a continuous vector field"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37859,
    "dDurationMs": 3831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tangent to a sphere must have at least one\npoint where the vector is zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41690,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what does this have to do with reality\napart from uncombable hairy balls?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45070,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the velocity of wind along the surface\nof the earth is a vector field, so the Hairy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49380,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ball Theorem guarantees that there's always\nat least one point on earth where the wind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53070,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't blowing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54070,
    "dDurationMs": 3070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it doesn't really matter that the object\nin question is ball-shaped."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57140,
    "dDurationMs": 4609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As long as it can be smoothly deformed into\na ball without cutting or sewing edges together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61749,
    "dDurationMs": 1181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the theorem still holds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62930,
    "dDurationMs": 4119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the next time a mathematician gives you\ntrouble, ask them if they can comb a hairy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67049,
    "dDurationMs": 151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "banana."
    } ]
  } ]
}
